      "statement": "In the universal Picard Fitting computation, the pullback of the Poincare bundle along a dual-number arc with tangent xi is, on the underlying curve, an extension of O_C by O_C with class xi (not an O_{C x D}-module extension with class xi tensor eps). Consequently the omega-twisted R^1 over the arc is 1-dimensional with eps acting by 0 and the Fitting ideal pulls back to (eps). Misreading the module structure yields a 3-dimensional cohomology and breaks the nonreduced inclusion I_e subset J. Future determinantal scheme-structure proofs reusing dual-number arcs must state this reading explicitly.",
      "status": "candidate",
      "summary": "In the universal Picard Fitting computation, the pullback of the Poincare bundle along a dual-number arc with tangent xi is, on the underlying curve, an extension of O_C by O_C with class xi (not an O_{C x D}-module extension with class xi tensor eps). Consequently the omega-twisted R^1 over the arc is 1-dimensional with eps acting by 0 and the Fitting ideal pulls back to (eps). Misreading the module structure yields a 3-dimensional cohomology and breaks the nonreduced inclusion I_e subset J. Future determinantal scheme-structure proofs reusing dual-number arcs must state this reading explicitly.",
